{
  "about": "Sew 0.7.2: the exact JSON tauri-plugin-sew-voice emits for a call that Sew ends and for SPEAK lost and given back. tests/contract.rs pins every payload to the wire types; tests/service.rs drives the fake engine (fake::FakeCall::end, fake::FakeCall::set_speak_denied) and checks the plugin emits these. Member ids are the tests' (self 48831765147549699, remote 48831765147549700); target and room are the tests' join arguments (k2:acme, 48831765147549698). Since 0.7.2 the state event and the state snapshot carry the call's target and room (absent while idle), and a moderator move sends a state event with the destination room (moved). Sew 0.7.3 adds recording consent (recording): a join into a recorded room is held at consent_required, with the notice in the recording event, until the consent command (or leave); the recording event follows the call's recording (null once none is active); the three recording leave reasons (ended.recording_reasons) end a call where declining means not joining.",
